  "id": "rmt",
  "term": "RMT",
  "definition": "RMT stands for Rasch Measurement Theory, an approach to improving psychological measurement by testing whether a questionnaire works as a single underlying scale, its items function independently and consistently, and response options are ordered as intended. It can also convert ordinal sum scores into interval-level latent trait scores to increase measurement precision.",
